<section class="evidence-band signal-chain-dossier larchive-dossier" aria-labelledby="larchive-product-heading">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>PRODUCT THEORY</p>
      <h2 id="larchive-product-heading">BEGIN WITH A TANGIBLE STORAGE AND DISPLAY OBJECT.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="link-list">
      <li>
        <h3>PRIMARY GOOD</h3>
        <p>A modular physical cartridge for storing and displaying one object with its identifier, viewing pane, removable tray, reversible mount, and provenance card.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>OPERATING DISCIPLINE</h3>
        <p>The protocol explains how the product is used: how an object enters, how revisions are marked, and how the physical cartridge remains tied to its record.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>DEFERRED EXTENSION</h3>
        <p>The digital index, Raspberry Pi display, RFID, and software layer come later. They support the product; they do not define the first public claim.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

